-- cmd: check
-- exit: 1
-- Of a type of one type argument, the mismatch of that argument is the
-- whole message: no note of the first argument, and no help of the
-- type's own (an Option's `?`) under a type constructor variable.
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: type mismatch: expected m(Int), got Option(String)
-- stderr-not-contains: is matched against the first type argument
-- stderr-not-contains: to chain through
fn double_all(xs: m(Int)) -> m(Int) { xs }
fn main() {
  println(double_all(Some("s")))
}
